Upstream-Status: Issue [https://github.com/dedupeio/dedupe/issues/1230]

BTrees 6.5 removed the long-deprecated byValue() method from every Bucket
and BTree family except II/LL, so CanopyIndex.search() raises
"AttributeError: 'BTrees.IFBTree.IFBucket' object has no attribute
'byValue'" on its IF results. This breaks dedupe 3.0.3 on every platform
with the current BTrees, and pypi.riseproject.dev only carries BTrees 6.5
for riscv64. Reimplement byValue(min) in Python: keep the entries whose
score is >= min, normalise each score by min when min > 0 (as the C
implementation does), and sort descending by (score, doc). Checked against
BTrees 6.3's byValue on random IFBucket/IFBTree data: identical key order,
scores equal up to the C code's float32 rounding.
--- a/dedupe/canopy_index.py
+++ b/dedupe/canopy_index.py
@@ -73,7 +73,15 @@
         results = mass_weightedUnion(L)
 
         qw = math.sqrt(qw)
-        filtered_results: list[tuple[float, int]] = results.byValue(qw * threshold)
+        min_score = qw * threshold
+        filtered_results: list[tuple[float, int]] = sorted(
+            (
+                (score / min_score if min_score > 0 else score, doc)
+                for doc, score in results.items()
+                if score >= min_score
+            ),
+            reverse=True,
+        )
 
         return filtered_results
 
